From c734a32b963558fba51889f0157e7bab6c801b11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:17:34 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 18f: expose extension actions and host action
 popups

Give the host the toolbar: per-tab snapshots of each enabled extension's action (title, badge text and colors, visibility, popup flag, wants-to-run and the icon at a requested scale through ExtensionActionIconFactory), change events from ExtensionActionDispatcher, ExtensionRegistry and icon loads, and a run call that is a toolbar click (ExtensionActionRunner::RunAction, granting activeTab). A popup is hosted as a new registry tab with view type kExtensionPopup in the extension's profile (spanning extensions use the original profile, as ExtensionViewHostFactory does): the shell attaches it like a tab, the renderer auto-resizes within Chromium's popup bounds and reports the size, and window.close() closes it. Popups record no history and get no tab identity. ABI 1.33 / bridge 0.35.0 (extension_actions); builds p81-p82, native list/badge/2x icon, activeTab onClicked scripting, popup attach/auto-resize/self-close and popup-tab rejection pass with local unpacked fixtures.

Last rebased: 2026-11-04 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
